<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:11:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🔴 Live: Deadly Russian attacks damage two bridges in Kyiv, mayor says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">b8fb8a8a-e4ae-11f1-9078-015da7f6db44</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:50:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Deadly Russian attacks damage two bridges in Kyiv, mayor says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description>
Russian attacks on Kyiv killed three people and damaged two bridges in the Ukrainian capital, city authorities said on Friday. The fresh wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" retaliation after Ukraine this week damaged the Crimea bridge. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c85c9ea-e4ab-11f1-a114-d3a799165f5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:32:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f85d74-e4ab-11f1-8758-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T015437Z-618531473-RC2DROAHQAD6-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Thomas Peter, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>FIFA: Infantino, Tashima and Diallo enter presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261120-fifa-infantino-tashima-and-diallo-enter-presidential-race</link><description>
Three candidates have officially submitted their bids for the FIFA presidency. Gianni Infantino, who has been in office for 11 years, is seeking a fourth consecutive term. Backed by UEFA, French Football Federation president Philippe Diallo wants to offer an alternative to Infantino’s leadership. He will face Japan’s Kohzo Tashima, honorary president of the Japan Football Association. The election will take place on March 18, 2027 in Rabat, Morocco.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5b836e4-e48b-11f1-946d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/fifa-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5b836e4-e48b-11f1-946d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/fifa-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea09638a-e48c-11f1-9920-d7a6c4b65e32</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:14:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Czechs protest en masse against 'concentration of power in one hand' and growing control over media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media</link><description>
As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Mikuláš Minář, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement, joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8a83266-e4a7-11f1-b6fc-0f49ce47132d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU and UK set to sign deals on trade, energy, youth mobility at Brussels summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit</link><description>
The UK and the EU are poised to agree new deals on trade, energy and youth mobility at a summit in Brussels on Friday, as part of UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's bid to reset ties with the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">215366b2-e486-11f1-8392-c54bec5a97cd</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:00:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/203b3d22-e486-11f1-9e19-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/c90a23b59a6d01ee8ae6acbb2cad20e56147ea25.jpg">© Carlos Jasso, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>White House fires national cyber director over widespread outages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages</link><description>
The White House fired national cyber director Sean Cairncross on Thursday following a week of technology disruptions affecting US air travel, email services and national security systems. The departure comes as the Trump administration faces criticism over its response to the outages, which officials say were unrelated incidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e56edbae-d878-11f1-8aa8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294693498447.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e56edbae-d878-11f1-8aa8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294693498447.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc3ce3ec-e481-11f1-a27b-e99dadc97588</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:28:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e56edbae-d878-11f1-8aa8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294693498447.jpg">© Evan Vucci, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>PM Sanchez admits 'mistakes' in key debate ahead of Spain's election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s%C3%A1nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election</link><description>
Spain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez acknowledged shortcomings in his government on Thursday as he faced conservative rival Alberto Nunez Feijoo in the campaign's only televised debate. The November 29 election could leave the far-right Vox party in a position to enter government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47a90c40-e47c-11f1-823f-bb1d3788691b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:49:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg">© Jaime Reina, Josep Lago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Voyager 1 spacecraft reaches one light-day milestone</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/voyager-1-spacecraft-reaches-one-light-day-milestone</link><description>
NASA's Voyager 1 probe, which has been traveling through space for nearly 50 years, hit a milestone distance of one light-day away from Earth on Wednesday. Already the most distant man-made object in the universe, the spacecraft is now about 26 billion kilometers (16 billion miles) away, according to the US space agency. That is the distance a particle of light can travel in 24 hours. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b60de9c0-e469-11f1-bc67-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-231241-231429-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b60de9c0-e469-11f1-bc67-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-231241-231429-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb85c36e-e469-11f1-abeb-eb5307a061fd</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:38:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Armed forces in Haiti kill at least 34 gang members to regain control of key corridor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members</link><description>
Haitian security forces launched a major offensive on Thursday to retake Martissant, a strategic corridor linking Port-au-Prince with the country's western and southern regions that gangs have controlled for five years. Police said at least 34 suspected gang members were killed in clashes involving a private security task force.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/181d54d6-e1f7-11f1-a490-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233346Z-695546907-RC24MOACBCCE-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/181d54d6-e1f7-11f1-a490-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233346Z-695546907-RC24MOACBCCE-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f515fb90-e468-11f1-b283-5bcaceac72d7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:31:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/181d54d6-e1f7-11f1-a490-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233346Z-695546907-RC24MOACBCCE-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg">© Fildor Pq Egeder, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Anthropic goes public after blockbuster IPO but fails to revive AI trade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261119-anthropic-goes-public-after-blockbuster-ipo-but-fails-to-revive-ai-trade</link><description>
Anthropic has become the first pure-play AI developer to be publicly traded on the stock market, following a record-setting IPO. The stock opened 34% higher, briefly valuing the company at more than $2 trillion, before ending its first day of trading up 17%. However, Wall Street indexes closed sharply lower as investors took profits, reflecting underlying market jitters about the AI trade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe47626a-e465-11f1-a3ac-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/4699281-US-Anthropic-IPO-Explainer-0-1080i50ESSENCE-23792.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe47626a-e465-11f1-a3ac-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/4699281-US-Anthropic-IPO-Explainer-0-1080i50ESSENCE-23792.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">299035d2-e466-11f1-8eab-d597055f8c05</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:22:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French far-left candidate Mélenchon opens door to alliance with rival Greens candidate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261119-melenchon-opens-door-to-alliance-with-french-greens-after-presidential-rival-overture-tondelier</link><description>
French far-left leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon opened the door to an alliance with France's Greens on Thursday after their presidential candidate Marine Tondelier said she was ready to "work on a coalition around" the veteran leftist. Tondelier's overture has further boosted Mélenchon's campaign for the Élysée Palace – and angered moderates on the centre-left.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fab2b82-e3a0-11f1-9252-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ED2CR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fab2b82-e3a0-11f1-9252-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ED2CR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e82e85a-e461-11f1-91c4-e93d56e35765</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:07:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fab2b82-e3a0-11f1-9252-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ED2CR.jpg">© Geoffroy Van Der Hasselt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan marathon champion banned for doping</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261119-kenyan-marathon-champion-banned-for-doping</link><description>
In tonight's edition, Kenyan athletics superstar and reigning marathon world champion Peres Jepchirchir is banned for three years for doping. Also, South African judges leave the courtroom behind and tour a repatriation centre before handing down judgment in 33 emergency asylum applications. And Ghana's presidency has a new jet, but critics of the ruling party are not on board.
</description><guid isPermaLink="false">dec457cc-e460-11f1-83ea-db85787c2904</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:38:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian strikes on Kyiv kill one, damage Dutch and Austrian embassies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies</link><description>
A wave of daytime Russian strikes on Kyiv on Thursday killed one person and damaged a historic cathedral as well as the embassies of Austria and the Netherlands. Loud explosions erupted across the Ukraine capital throughout the day as the leaders of Russia, China and the United States held a historic meeting in China that put Russia's President Vladimir Putin in international spotlight. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5eb9e890-e45f-11f1-ab0f-8dbb507a1f19</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:25:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We're seeing in real time the effects that AI is going to have on cybersecurity', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/we-re-seeing-in-real-time-the-effects-that-ai-is-going-to-have-on-cybersecurity-expert-says</link><description>
FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Dr. R. David Edelman, Senior Fellow at the Brookings Institution, also former Director for Cybersecurity on the National Security Council under the Obama administration. He explains that the latest spate of network outages shows "in real time the effects that AI is going to have on cybersecurity" adding that "the one thing that's tying most of these outages together is that companies and institutions are racing to patch a system that's been identified as vulnerable, and they're patching what themselves are pretty creaky digital systems".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bed7beae-e45b-11f1-9cd8-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-210356-211312-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bed7beae-e45b-11f1-9cd8-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-210356-211312-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4174fe2-e45b-11f1-93dd-97fc8684d39e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:06:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kushner says Trump 'open' to extend NATO mutual defense-type clause to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine</link><description>
US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday that President Donald Trump was open to extending to Ukraine a security guarantee similar to NATO's mutual defense clause, but stressed that Washington has to protect its interests too. The comments came as German Chancellor Friedrich Merz qualified the summit between the presidents of the United States, Russia and China as a "photo op". FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator Douglas Herbert explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e2b59d8-e452-11f1-b9df-1b5e5e3e7684</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron urges Ukraine's allies to 'reopen the question' of NATO membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called for Ukraine's allies to speed up the delivery of urgently needed air defence systems and urged them to "reopen the question" of Ukraine's NATO membership after talks in Berlin aimed at reaffirming European support for Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4326a9aa-e456-11f1-8321-2f542a93f4a9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:32:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg">© Hannah McKay, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>A president among body bags: Photo ops spark outrage in Colombia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia</link><description>
Since taking office in August, Colombia's far-right President Abelardo de la Espriella has regularly posted videos that show him walking among body bags supposedly holding the remains of rebel fighters – a communications strategy that has sparked widespread criticism. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa71908-d878-11f1-b19e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2-Colombie-pst-sacs-mortuaires-2septembre.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa71908-d878-11f1-b19e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2-Colombie-pst-sacs-mortuaires-2septembre.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3701a06-dded-11f1-9b12-edf15fb436e4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:52:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Three of a kind? Xi hosts Trump and Putin as Ukraine war grinds on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on</link><description>
Gang of three or glorified photo op? Xi Jinping hosting Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Already, our Monday panel rejected attempts to paint the three-way meeting as a new Yalta, as in the 1945 sit-down on the Black Sea that defined the post-war security architecture of Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c65e57fc-e44a-11f1-91b0-ff7f8e5d3944</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:39:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Xi-Trump-Putin trilateral meeting: Trump's recognition of China and Russia as 'peers of the US'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/xi-trump-putin-trilateral-meeting-trump-s-recognition-of-china-and-russia-as-peers-of-the-us</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Olivia Cheung. The trilateral meeting between Donald Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin at the APEC summit was significant despite the absence of concrete agreements, according to Cheung. “The significance is seen in the precedence of the United States seeing and giving recognition that China and Russia are peers of the United States,” she explained, adding that “the image of a G3 is very significant.”
